.. _{{ ref }} prerequisites:

Prerequisites
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

What you need, depends on what you are trying to do. As a minimum, you need to
start out with:

Hardware prerequisites
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

#. The :adi:`{{ som | upper }} <en/resources/evaluation-hardware-and-software/evaluation-boards-kits/{{ som }}.html>`
   system-on-module
#. The :adi:`{{ carrier | upper }} <en/resources/evaluation-hardware-and-software/evaluation-boards-kits/{{ carrier }}.html>`
   carrier board, with the power supply and USB cables that come with it
#. Host PC (Windows or Linux)
#. Ethernet cable, and a network with a DHCP server, to load Linux from the
   host PC
#. Optional: an external ICE, such as the ICE-1000 or ICE-1500, if the on-board
   debug agent is not used (see :ref:`adsp-jtag`)

Software prerequisites
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

#. The ADI fork of OpenOCD, built as described in :ref:`adsp setup`
#. A GDB that supports the ARM architecture (``gdb-multiarch`` on
   Ubuntu/Debian)
#. UART terminal application (PuTTY/TeraTerm/Minicom), 115200 8N1
#. Python 3, to serve the Linux images to U-Boot over HTTP
#. Optional: :adi:`CrossCore Embedded Studio <cces-quickstart>` and the
   {{ som | upper }} Board Support Package (BSP), for baremetal and RTOS
   development

.. _{{ ref }} quickstart:

Quick start
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This quick start sets up the {{ som | upper }} on the {{ carrier | upper }}
carrier board, with JTAG through the on-board debug agent. The software steps,
OpenOCD, U-Boot and Linux, are described in :ref:`adsp setup`; this section
covers the board specific settings.

Hardware setup
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Disconnect all power before changing switches and jumpers, or inserting the
SoM.

.. include-template:: {{ templates }}som-setup.rst.jinja
   :file: {{ boards }}{{ som }}.yaml

.. include-template:: {{ templates }}carrier-setup.rst.jinja
   :file: {{ boards }}{{ carrier }}.yaml

The sections :ref:`{{ som | upper }} <{{ ref }} som>` and
:ref:`{{ carrier | upper }} <{{ ref }} carrier>` describe all the switches and
jumpers used above.

Software setup
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Follow :ref:`adsp setup`, with these settings:

#. Start OpenOCD with the debug agent interface and the target configuration of
   the {{ processor }}:

   .. shell:: sh

      ~/openocd
      $ sudo src/openocd -f {{ openocd_interface }} \
             -f {{ openocd_target }} \
             --search tcl/ \
             --search tcl/interface/ \
             --search tcl/target/

#. Open the serial console of the SoM at 115200 8N1.
#. Download and extract the ``{{ release }}`` release, load U-Boot with GDB,
   and boot Linux with the ``{{ dtb }}`` device tree.
#. Optionally install U-Boot to the flash and Linux to the eMMC.

